{"name":"Fennec Fox","hex":"#dad7c8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fennec fox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fennec."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fennec_fox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fennec fox","blocks":[{"text":"The fennec fox is a small fox native to the deserts of North Africa, ranging from Western Sahara and Mauritania to the Sinai Peninsula. Its most distinctive feature is its unusually large ears, which serve to dissipate heat and listen for underground prey. The fennec is the smallest fox species. Its coat, ears, and kidney functions have adapted to the desert environment with high temperatures and little water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Fennec_Fox_Vulpes_zerda.jpg/330px-Fennec_Fox_Vulpes_zerda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fennec_fox","wikidata":"Q131564"},{"title":"Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Foxes are small-to-medium-sized omnivorous mammals belonging to several genera of the family Canidae. They have a flattened skull; upright, triangular ears; a pointed, slightly upturned snout; and a long, bushy tail (\"brush\")."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg/330px-Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox","wikidata":"Q8331"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Fennecus_zerda_05_MWNH_1387.JPG/500px-Fennecus_zerda_05_MWNH_1387.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Fennecus_zerda_05_MWNH_1387.JPG/1280px-Fennecus_zerda_05_MWNH_1387.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Fennecus_zerda_05_MWN